ith the row and column popcounts cached. So","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"members(ofHyperedgeAt:)"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedges(of:)"},{"text":" are each one ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BitSet"},{"text":" copy of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"⌈n\/64⌉ or ⌈m\/64⌉ words, a cell edit writes two bits in O(1), and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"transposed()"},{"text":", the dual,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"swaps the two in O(1). The cost is 2·n·m\/8 bytes: ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"the matrix is for dense or small","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidence","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" (spectral work at n·m up to about 10⁹, hypergraphs with large hyperedges). Sparse","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"incidence belongs in ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Equality compares cell for cell, with equal shape: column order is observable, because a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"column’s position is what a spectral caller indexes by. (","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedIncidenceList","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s equality","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ignores positions; convert to compare that way.)","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/incidencematrixmodule\/incidencematrix"]}],"references":{"doc://IncidenceMatrixModule/documentation/IncidenceMatrixModule/IncidenceMatrix/appendVertex()":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Appends a vertex with no memberships, a zero row."}],"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"appendVertex","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind